WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.420
It's March.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:08.980
The seasons have turned, and the spring bloom will soon return to the cold, clear ocean waters. {## even if she's only talking about the one season, that's just how this works / 'changed' if you're not attached to this, but you probably are}

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.000
It is also the biggest crossroads of the year for those of us in high school.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.910
Our third-year senpai are setting off for their own futures,

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.910
and new underclassmen are coming to take their places. {## could be 'kouhai'}

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.710
It's a special season when both we and the sea are preparing for spring.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.100
Ah, it's my number!

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.280
Mine too!

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.650
You both passed! {## I'm still waiting for the day when I see someone not pass in an anime}{maybe watch more anime, perhaps slow start?}

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:56.700
Oh? So Teko-chan, you completed your underwater navigation course too.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.780
Yes.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.330
The last required topic is deep diving.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.820
And after deep diving, all that's left is one final elective.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.010
Only one left...

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.810
You worked hard to get here, Teko.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.380
Yeah.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.840
And then you'll get your Advanced License at last.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:19.140
Start thinking now about what you want your last elective to be.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.640
<i>I only have one left.</i>

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:29.310
<i>With each step I take, I get a little bit closer to the end.</i>

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.710
<i>I'm happy, but also somewhat sad. {## 'mournful' is really like, death. and don't tell me this is figurative death, I'm not having it}</i>

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.240
<i>Those feelings repeat as I move forward.</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.070
<i>That's just how it is.</i>

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.960
<i>Deep diving.</i>

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.540
<i>Due to the elevated water pressure, 
your mental faculties become sluggish. {## WHAT is the 5's stroke order, the bottom first? what the hell?}{it's the CORRECT way, you do the bottom stroke first}</i>

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:56.220
<i>It's a harsh environment that forces you to increase your air 
consumption, limiting you to 10 minutes at the max of 40 meters.</i>

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.240
<i>Man, look at the joy on her face.</i>

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:26.240
<i>It feels like only yesterday that Pikari had to lead her everywhere by the hand.</i>

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.330
<i>But now, Teko is forging onward of her own will. {## or 'with'}</i>

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.870
<i>She really has grown.</i>

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.020
<i>It's a mambo! {yes}</i>

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.070
<i>Can I really borrow your camera?</i>

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.150
<i>What are these fish?</i>

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.710
<i>They're adorable! {## man, every time}</i>

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.590
Teko, well done.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.300
Thank you!

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.800
The ocean was really generous to us today.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.030
That mambo!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.190
Exactly! You hardly ever get the chance to see them.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.040
There were lots of oval squid too. {## why are all these}

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.610
Also, those tiny, adorable fish!

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.530
The baby lumpfish. {## English when mambou}

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.680
They call the pattern on their heads an angel halo. {## Ane, what are you doing}

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.010
I can see why!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.640
Did you get any good pictures?

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.830
I almost forgot.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.810
I hope they came out well.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:23.830
Well, you know... Underwater photography is pretty hard.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.700
I was hoping I'd done a better job...

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:37.170
In that case, do you want to take underwater photography as your final elective?

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:42.670
Actually, I... {## laretil looc / if not this, 'I've already decided.': 'picked' sounds like filed the paperwork and she has regrets}

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.090
I want to do night diving.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.430
Teko?

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.030
Are you sure?

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.060
Yes, I can do it!

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.690
I didn't think you'd end up choosing night diving.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.690
D-Do you think I'm being reckless?

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:09.700
Not at all. It's just a bit unexpected.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.230
I'm happy you feel that it's unexpected. {## reasons: 'it's' can parse as 'its' or 'it's' here because of the feel [noun] [adj] structure}

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:16.210
Oh yeah?

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.980
You're the one who told me.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.590
You can't change others or the past,

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.520
but you can change yourself and the future.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:31.430
<i>Oh man, she's giving me the warm fuzzies!</i>

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:36.620
The words you said back then gave me a push. {## 'words were what ...' asserts a focus on that object existing, you know what I mean? like 'gave me a push [no ha] those words', but that's inappropriate here}

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.440
They inspired me to change.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.350
Sensei, you really said something great. {## same as katori talking herself up in previous episodes}

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.700
Yumegaoka High School Diving Club, at attention!

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.770
What's going on?

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.870
All of us will be attending Teko's last course dive.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.970
Whoa, that sounds like a good time!

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:00.660
Right?

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.510
C'mon, c'mon! Let's-a go!

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.090
Thanks, Teko-chan!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.270
I'm sorry for the trouble!

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:11.470
Yeah?

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.930
And so that's why you want me to come too.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:21.980
Yep. After all, it'll be a big accomplishment 
for Teko, so we should all be around to celebrate.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:25.500
Grandma, I'm taking the laundry home with me.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.450
Got it. Thanks, Kodama.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:31.230
Kodama-chan's coming too, 
and I couldn't be more excited!

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.080
What? I never said I'd be going.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:40.580
But, but, but! You got into Yumegaoka, 
and you're joining the Diving Club, right?

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.130
Deliberations are still ongoing. {## orig sounds like 'it's not yet disqualified', a positive, instead of 'I haven't yet decided for that', the appropriate negative}

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.840
I'm going to do what I want to do most.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:49.030
Kotori will probably go to see Teko-san though. {## I'm reading this as 'Kotori will go to the diving' for the next line but it wasn't clear as that before (potentially being 'Kotori will join the club', and that goes for all these lines)}

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:53.470
Right? And that means you'll come to cheer Teko on too, right? {## i initially read this as 'join diving club to cheer Teko on (???)', e.g.}

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.470
If Kotori's going, I won't not consider it.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.940
I'll take that as an okay! I'll invite Kokoro-chan too!

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.990
Looks like the whole gang'll be there.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.390
And as such, Grandma...

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.160
I have a little request to ask of you.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:08.900
What's that?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.120
You got it!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.990
Yay! We're gonna have a blast!

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:27.060
Be careful not to get sick before we go night diving.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.150
I will.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.640
After I finish, I'll be getting my Advanced License.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.640
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.100
What's up? Still feeling anxious?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.600
No, not exactly.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.610
What, you feeling down? {## what on earth, 'morose'?}

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:50.570
It's like I'm kind of sad, but not really, but maybe lonely...

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:57.330
I want to get my license as soon as possible so I can dive with Pikari and the others even more.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:02.100
I'm excited thinking about all the fun things we'll get to do.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.040
But...

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.710
We keep leaving all these fun things behind us.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:12.340
So I thought I just had to keep finding even more fun things to do.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.300
But...

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.820
Even those will someday come to an end.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:21.770
I've been trying not to think about it,

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:25.020
but every time something fun comes to an end,

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.980
it pops back into my head.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.450
I don't know what I'm supposed to do!

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.740
What should I do about it? {## time loop}

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:39.640
The thing is...

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.080
Nobody knows. {## the yuru yuris know}

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:46.040
But that's what we call youth.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.660
That's the way it should be.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:54.970
It's fine if you don't know. Instead,

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.420
be sure to keep on moving.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:01.120
If you stop, you'll never figure it out.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.770
Youth is the best!

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.770
Th-Thank you for your advice!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:19.830
<i>A time will come when you'll be inspired to do it.</i>

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:23.580
<i>I'll look forward to the day we get to go night diving! {## I'm not checking these, so I hope you did}</i>

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.510
<i>Dear Fun Expert,</i>

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:35.680
<i>do you think you'll be able to find something else fun after we go night diving? {## 'beyond' just, it doesn't make sense}</i>

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.470
<i>If you ask me...</i>

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.350
<i>Upyo-pyo-pyo-pyo! It's a secret!</i>

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.130
<i>Ah, I'm way too excited!</i>

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:47.830
<i>Pikari's secrets always contain fun.</i>

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:51.320
<i>Yeah, I just have to enjoy it with all my heart.</i>

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.650
<i>I'm honestly still a little scared of night diving,</i>

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.670
<i>but I plan to enjoy every second.</i>

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:01.500
<i>I'm looking forward to it!</i>

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:11.040
Um, why...

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.140
The surprise guests!

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.000
Introducing the Teko Cheer Squad!

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.800
I had Grandma secretly drive them over.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.640
This was your secret? {## ain't no more, is it}

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:27.200
Grandmother, Kodama-chan, and Kotori-chan.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:29.430
Even Kokoro-chan is here.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.900
Y-Yeah.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:34.330
They're more of a Cheer and Send-Off Squad. {## quoth MW, and I'm in favour of full capsing with hyphens, as you know}

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.400
I really appreciate all this!

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.780
Teko-chan, you just keep on moving forward.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:43.250
I will!

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:48.330
I can't believe it...

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.450
Me neither...

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.460
Can't believe what?

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:55.510
I think they can't believe that anyone would dive into that black sea at night. {## hmph}

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.170
Oh yeah?

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:06.450
Um, will you be all right?

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:07.050
Huh?

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.350
I mean, the ocean is so dark.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.110
You're asking if I'm scared? {## must be negative for greater contrast with later affirmative (see: 'kowakunai', in partic) / also the original is an abomination, and it'd need some weird reworking and quotation marks to fix}

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:12.060
Yes...

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.270
I <i>am</i> scared!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:17.640
Last time, I was so scared that I stayed on land. {## repeat good}

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.940
Like I thought!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:25.260
But over time, those feelings of fear were overcome by the desire to give it a try. {## 'overcome with' means the feelings of fear wanted to go diving}

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:33.330
Even if you feel so scared you think you'll never do 
something, there may come a day when you can handle it.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.950
Th-That's so cool, Teko-san!

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.760
Thanks...

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.480
Teko, let's do our buddy check.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:43.640
Coming!

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.230
I'll go first.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.870
Please do.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.610
BC check... OK. {I don't know why they dropped the BCD this season}{## I feel like this was 'okay' before, so it'll probably have to be looked at in batch}

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:56.020
<i>It's all thanks to Pikari that I can handle it now.</i>

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:56.020
Weight check...

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.010
All done. Please go ahead, Teko.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.580
Got it. BC check... OK. {## of course I support 'OK' though}

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.870
Weight check... OK.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.880
That looks so cool, and it seems like fun.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.120
There's no way diving into those dark waters won't be scary.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.740
All right, let's head out.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.520
Okay!

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.770
Take care!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.020
See you later!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:41.780
Good luck, Teko.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:43.900
Thanks!

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.660
Y-You heard that? {## you said it at like full volume kid}

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.810
Your wish to go night diving someday is already coming true.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.040
Yeah.

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:04.380
<i>I accomplished my goal of making this wish come true in almost no time.</i>

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:09.350
<i>My excitement and sadness ebb and flow like the waves.</i>

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:14.000
<i>And today, those waves feel very pleasant.</i>

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:22.260
Okay, let's go, Teko.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.280
Right.

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:31.410
It's so pretty.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:38.540
There's a saying that goes that seeing night divers off makes you want to try it yourself. {## what kind of shitty fucking saying / you won't find that in Proverbs}

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.880
I think that might be true.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.510
It'd be a waste to lose to the fear.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.470
That so?

00:13:56.700 --> 00:14:02.870
<i>Just like Pikari told me, the ocean illuminated at night isn't the usual blue world.</i>

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:08.190
<i>It's like we're not even in the sea at all!</i>

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.470
<i>Um...</i>

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.210
<i>Flying?</i>

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.880
<i>Oh, I got it!</i>

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:25.170
<i>She's saying that it looks like Ane-chan-senpai and the others are flying in the sky.</i>

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:30.050
<i>The colors are the same as they are on land, 
so the water looks more like air.</i>

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:33.890
<i>I thought the same thing the first time I did this.</i>

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:40.940
<i>The way her emotions overflow and show on her face one after the other is the cutest part of Teko.</i>

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:43.800
<i>It's like Teko's feelings</i>

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.400
<i>are flowing into me through the ocean!</i>

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.780
<i>"Wonderful. Fun. Mysterious."</i>

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.740
<i>"I'm not scared anymore."</i>

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.570
<i>"I'm fine now!"</i>

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:57.060
<i>I can feel them all!</i>

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:03.900
<i>Yeah, it really is pretty!</i>

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:11.270
<i>Lit by sparkling spotlights, they dance upon the stage of the sea like water fairies, undines!</i>

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.140
<i>This is just like...</i>

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.170
<i>a fantasy world! {## alt. 'DisneySea'}</i>

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.790
<i>Not too long ago, she looked on the verge of tears...</i>

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:27.960
<i>She was so afraid...</i>

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:36.050
<i>My buddy is so strongly and beautifully swimming forward.</i>

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:44.530
The lights are disappearing!

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.120
Did something go wrong?

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:51.630
The spring bloom came earlier than usual this year.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.090
What happens when it's early?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.890
The ocean will give a gift to Teko-chan.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.060
<i>This should be long enough.</i>

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.740
<i>It's a pitch-black world of darkness.</i>

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.430
<i>But you'll be okay.</i>

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:16.700
<i>We'll begin once our eyes have adjusted.</i>

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:28.400
<i>Countless plankton react to the movements of our arms and legs, emitting a faint light.</i>

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:35.300
<i>The true name of the tiny lights that sparkle like fireflies is </i>Noctiluca scintillans<i>! {now under other circumstances I may have gone for "sea sparkle", but this is the most obvious scientific name I've ever read}{## binoms are itald}</i>

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.260
<i>I get you, I get you!</i>

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:46.660
<i>Thanks to Teko, I've been able to remember what it was like when I first started diving.</i>

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:54.340
<i>My ambiguous feelings are given color and form.</i>

00:16:55.740 --> 00:17:01.180
<i>Teko is the key that opens the door to my memories and feelings! {## X to the Y of Z is just too long a chain}</i>

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:05.850
<i>I hope I can thank her eloquently some day. {## not likely, upyopyopyo}</i>

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:12.710
They're back.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:16.530
Is that pork soup?

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:17.770
Yay!

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:21.520
This is my surprise, straight from Amanchu House!

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:22.980
You're the best, Grandma!

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:24.480
I'm so happy!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.710
It smells delicious.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.020
What's up, Teko?

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.550
Take those heavy tanks off first.

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.900
No, it's nothing.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:30.900
Okay!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.150
So warm!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:36.570
Kino-san is an angel!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.970
Um, Teko-san.

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:39.740
Yeah?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.790
Was it as scary as you thought?

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.120
Not at all.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.180
Not one little bit!

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:54.510
Because of the light, all the colors were the same as usual, so all the fish and divers looked like they were flying. {## not a direct quote, and I just... don't like 'same as on land', but I can't extend it like I did the earlier}

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.890
It was like a stage in the sea lit by sparkling spotlights.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:03.700
Everyone seemed like water fairies, undines, dancing in the sky! {## 'in the sky like undines' is weird because undines don't fly}

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.300
It was just like a fantasy world!

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:09.210
<i>I can't believe we were thinking exactly the same thing! {## great minds think alike, so I guess the other ones do too}</i>

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.240
<i>No, no, no!</i>

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:12.690
Pikari?

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:18.320
All right, Teko. You are now officially the holder of an Advanced License.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:19.910
Yes!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.600
Congratulations!

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:22.740
Thank you!

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.740
We'll have to take a celebratory diving trip.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:27.830
Oh! You mean to the place Kino-san discovered! {they remember Teko wanting to go}

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:32.240
I want to go! And to the Dragon Palace too!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.670
Teko, sounds like there'll be no time to be sad.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.990
Right!

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:40.170
There are plenty of fun things waiting ahead of us!

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:43.940
Yeah, but that's not all.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:51.610
I've realized that fun and sadness 
ebb and flow over and over like waves.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:52.990
Like waves...

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:54.230
Yes.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:57.070
Again and again.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:02.590
There may be days when the water is calm, but new waves will always come. {## I don't want to say 'ebb and flow' again, and further it's weird to say 'a wave comes to ebb and flow', because reasons}

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:04.810
So we'll be okay no matter what.

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:12.370
Huh, wait... Am I not making sense again?

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:13.770
Don't you worry.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:14.880
I understand as well. {## too too}

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:19.910
That's amazing, Teko. Now I feel like everything'll work out too.

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:20.890
Really?

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.050
Isn't it mysterious?

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:22.840
Yeah.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:28.770
Being able to think like that is just proof of how strong you two have grown.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:29.730
Right, Kino-san?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.190
Yeah, that's right. They deserve praise.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:41.440
With that said, if a wave of sadness is too big, I feel like I may sink again.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.780
That's nothing to worry about.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:49.100
It's true that the more fun you have, the sadder you feel when it's over.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:59.630
But take it the other way, and the sadder you are 
one day, the bigger the next wave of fun will feel.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.490
So it'll all work out. {## work out into an ever increasingly violent pattern of swings, yeah}

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.940
Even if you go your separate ways.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.850
You'll be just fine.

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:16.770
I...

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.390
I want to join the Diving Club! {## MISTAKE, GO FOR LIGHT MUSIC}

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:22.470
Huh?! Then... me too. {## BANDWAGONER}

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:31.810
Meetings and separations, huh.

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:34.920
It feels like it's been a while.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.870
It's the beginning of a new year.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:44.550
There are graduates, there are new students, and there's me, able to grow one year older. {## THIS WAS DUMB ENOUGH DURING THE ARC}

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:47.260
I'm grateful to you, Mato-chan. {## DON'T BRING IT UP EVERY TIME THIS GUY SHOWS UP FROM NOW ON}

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.740
Meetings and separations are like waves that ebb and flow too.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:51.400
Huh?

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.900
The sadder the separation, the happier the next meeting.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.870
Right... Did something happen?

00:20:58.870 --> 00:20:59.860
Not particularly.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:03.400
Just thinking about what we can teach our students. {## HOW ABOUT WHAT'S ON THE ENTRANCE EXAM}

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.820
Uh... right.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:14.370
We're in the same class again this year! I'm really happy!

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.750
Yeah, me too!

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:21.740
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:19.700
So, the thing is...

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:24.000
I wrote about my feelings of gratitude for you in a letter.

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:26.980
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.030
What?!

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:25.790
Huh?!

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.150
I actually did too!

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:34.730
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:27.760
Upyo!

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:31.340
Can I read it now?

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.410
Should I wait?

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.730
Go ahead...

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:42.940
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:39.700
"Dear Teko.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.590
Thank you for meeting me.

00:21:42.590 --> 00:21:45.410
Thank you for picking up diving.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:48.430
It can't be explained with words

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:48.290
Thank you for working hard for your Advanced License.

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:57.320
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:53.360
And thank you in advance for continuing to be friends with me.

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:58.270
Let me know about places you want to go or things you want to do. {## anywhere anywhere}

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.770
I'll take you anywhere."

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:04.120
The days have begun to get shorter now

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:12.250
Why must they cut off my time with you?

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:07.500
Is it okay if I read yours too?

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:09.010
Go ahead!

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:11.900
"Dear Pikari.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:15.890
Thank you for meeting me one year ago.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:17.820
Tomorrow and the day after, and every day forevermore

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:18.890
Thank you for giving me a nickname.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:22.970
I want to keep walking home together like this

00:22:18.890 --> 00:22:21.810
Thank you for inviting me to start diving.

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:26.720
And thank you in advance for everything you'll continue to show me.

00:22:22.970 --> 00:22:28.450
No matter what the weather was, no matter how my day went

00:22:27.770 --> 00:22:34.460
Please take me to Grandmother's wonderful spot and the Dragon Palace and many more places."

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:36.190
The moment you raise your hand to wave goodbye

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:44.840
I feel like it has been a wonderful day

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:40.350
Pikari.

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:42.080
Yeah?

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:46.520
I'm so happy right now!

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:49.080
So am I, Teko.

00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:58.950
It's now the beginning of April.

00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:01.950
Teko's wish came true right away.

00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:06.610
Her next wish is to come back with Kodama-chan and Kotori-chan!

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:11.870
It's been true this year, and will be forevermore...

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:14.860
Fun is endless!
